From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:39:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: clock: describe the T8011 touch clock

T8011 reuses the T8010 gate/divider at PMGR offset 0x78000. Describe its compatible with the existing T8010 fallback.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/clk/0010-dt-bindings-clock-describe-the-T8011-touch-clock.patch; rebased onto main, otherwise unchanged.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml    | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml
index f49ce6014..277d877b4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml
@@ -14,7 +14,8 @@ description:
   reference clock consumed by the touchscreen controller. The S8000 PMGR has
   the same block at the same offset; the iPad 5 N1 touchscreen runs it at
   32768 Hz. So has the T8015 PMGR, whose iPhone X touchscreen runs it at
-  24 MHz.
+  24 MHz. The T8011 PMGR also uses this block at offset 0x78000; its J120
+  touchscreen runs from the 24 MHz reference.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -25,6 +26,7 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - enum:
               - apple,s8000-touch-clock
+              - apple,t8011-touch-clock
               - apple,t8015-touch-clock
           - const: apple,t8010-touch-clock
 
